  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 141,
    "summary": "David pleads with the Lord to hear his prayers—The reproof of the righteous is a kindness.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Lord, I cry unto thee: make haste unto me; give ear unto my voice, when I cry unto thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Ps. 70:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let my prayer be set forth before thee as incense; and the lifting up of my hands as the evening sacrifice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Rev. 5:8 (1–10)."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Ex. 30:7; 37:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "Ex. 29:41 (38–42)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 54
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Set a watch, O Lord, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Ps. 39:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Incline not my heart to any evil thing, to practise wicked works with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the righteous smite me; it shall be a kindness: and let him reprove me; it shall be an excellent oil, which shall not break my head: for yet my prayer also shall be in their calamities.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Ps. 141:5 When the righteous smite me with the word of the Lord it is a kindness; and when they reprove me, it shall be an excellent oil, and shall not destroy my faith; for yet my prayer also shall be for them. I delight not in their calamities."
          },
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Prov. 27:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Prov. 9:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 87
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 111
          },
          {
            "start": 160,
            "end": 168
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When their judges are overthrown in stony places, they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "IE the righteous."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Our bones are scattered at the grave’s mouth, as when one cutteth and cleaveth wood upon the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Ezek. 6:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But mine eyes are unto thee, O God the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave not my soul destitute.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Ps. 25:15; D&C 4:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Keep me from the snares which they have laid for me, and the gins of the workers of iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
